Subject: the desktop binds Ctrl + wheel to the Raye desktop menu by default

Ctrl + wheel on the desktop resizes the icons, the way it does on
Windows. The action is a containment action, and libplasma reads a
desktop's bindings from this shell package's `defaults`, section
[Desktop][ContainmentActions] -- the same place the right click menu and
the middle click paste are declared. Raye's binding joins them.

So every account gets it from the shell package: a new one and one made
a year ago alike, with nothing written into anybody's configuration and
no script going round to fix accounts afterwards.

🚨 It replaces a per-account write that was wrong. Raye wrote the key
into [ActionPlugins][<containment id>], but libplasma reads
[ActionPlugins][<containment TYPE>] -- `QString::number((int)
containmentType())`, where Desktop is 0 and Panel is 1, and the
settings module writes it the same way. A desktop containment's id is
rarely 0, so the binding was written where nothing reads it and
Ctrl + wheel did nothing at all.

⚠️ And correcting that id to 0 would have been worse than the bug: a
[ActionPlugins][0] group holding only this one key makes libplasma skip
the whole defaults block, so the desktop would have lost its right
click menu and its middle click paste. A default read from the package
has no such edge.

Reason: this cannot be done outside the source. `defaults` is a file of
this shell package, owned by plasma-desktop; shipping a second copy of
it from another package is a file conflict, not a configuration. And
the per-account alternatives are what this replaces: a login script
that runs forever to patch accounts one by one, and a layout script
that only ever runs once, for an account that does not exist yet.

--- a/desktoppackage/contents/defaults
+++ b/desktoppackage/contents/defaults
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 [Desktop][ContainmentActions]
 RightButton;NoModifier=org.kde.contextmenu
 MiddleButton;NoModifier=org.kde.paste
+wheel:Vertical;ControlModifier=org.raye.desktopmenu
 
 [Panel]
 Containment=org.kde.panel
